["er.eventlog.import-anchor/1",{"authority":{"logical_scope":"aep","stream_identity":"01a0cae6-7e88-710c-8913-d70d29cb7b4c","tenant":"planning"},"completeness":"available_evidence_only","evidence":[],"instance":{"entity":"aep.entity","fields":{"document":{"events":[],"fields":{"$aep":{"archived":false,"metadata":{"created_at":0,"id":"MIG8cdaf0b623597c5bcde0111ae7cf65490eaad4dd33babdc5dbedb06e2140e5cb","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/authoritative-gate-status","provenance":{"created_by":"system","updated_by":"system"},"revision":4,"type":"aep.story/v1","updated_at":0}},"body":"## Finding\n\nThe workflow and Taskfile independently enumerate verification, while reader-facing prose repeats versions, component delivery and gate claims that have drifted from tags, the store and the tree.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nCI invokes `task check` after provisioning its declared environment, and release verification reuses that entry point. `cargo xtask status --check` owns every generated volatile status region. Hand-maintained current-state claims become links to annotated-tag status, the planning store or gap register. A drift test fails if CI stops invoking the gate or a generated region changes.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `.github/workflows/`, `Taskfile.yml`, `xtask/` and generated status regions — cited.\n- README, VISION, reconciliation and website status prose — inferred from the review search; confirm each claim before editing.\n","relations":[{"derived_from":"epic:architecture-hardening"},{"serves":"vision:O6"}],"status":"implemented","summary":"Remove a second CI gate and hand-maintained current-state claims.","title":"CI and prose derive from the executable gate and durable status sources"},"lifecycle_state":"implemented"}},"id":"MIG8cdaf0b623597c5bcde0111ae7cf65490eaad4dd33babdc5dbedb06e2140e5cb","lifecycle_state":"recorded","revision":4,"version":1},"order":"per_kind_only","subject":["aep.entity","MIG8cdaf0b623597c5bcde0111ae7cf65490eaad4dd33babdc5dbedb06e2140e5cb"]}]